---
import Layout from '../../components/Layout.astro';
import CostCalculator from '../../islands/CostCalculator';
---

<Layout
  title="Cost per gram of active"
  description="Convert a bottle price into cost per gram of elemental or active compound — the number the label never gives you. Magnesium oxide is ~60% elemental; glycinate ~14%."
>
  <div class="tool-head">
    <h1>Cost per gram of active</h1>
    <p>
      A bottle price tells you what a serving of a <i>compound form</i> costs. What you're
      buying is the elemental or active fraction — and that ranges from over 85% (creatine
      monohydrate) down to 7% (magnesium threonate). This converts label numbers into the
      one that matters. Two magnesium rows are preloaded as a worked example — the cheaper
      bottle loses — with invented prices, not prices from any shop.
    </p>
  </div>
  <CostCalculator client:load />
</Layout>

<style>
  .tool-head { padding: 32px 0 20px; max-width: 680px; }
  h1 { font-size: 24px; font-weight: 800; margin: 0 0 10px; }
  p { font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.55; color: var(--body-2); text-wrap: pretty; }
</style>
